 # State Schema
 
+## Coupled status ownership
+
+The `spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH` command reads the native coupled-run manifest and durable iteration ledgers. Request counts belong to the durable ledger writer: `wire_requests` counts every request entry, while `task_requests` counts task-charged entries and applies the native default when charge is omitted. Pending interrupted usage may be unknown when its ledger is absent; the command reports null rather than zero. The recorded completion status belongs to the native manifest and is not independent verification or promotion authorization.
+
+
 This document defines the main state surfaces in `spiral-coder` and which layer
 owns each kind of data.
 
